+# Makes what the realistic view draws with, the first time it is chosen.
+function prepare bim realistic drawing on {pointer:window}:
+    execute:
+        ensure gpu realistic drawing in (the gpu context of window)
+
+# Whether the 3D view draws realistically from this frame on, and whether
+# the sun's shadow map holds the model (parameters 62 and 63).
+function set bim realistic drawing {boolean:isRealistic} shadowed {boolean:hasShadowMap} on {pointer:window}:
+    execute:
+        set context to the gpu context of window
+        set gpu realistic drawing to isRealistic in context
+        set holder to @intrinsic("dereference", context)
+        set flag to 0.0
+        if isRealistic:
+            set flag to 1.0
+        set gpu parameter 62 to flag in holder
+        set mapFlag to 0.0
+        if isRealistic and hasShadowMap:
+            set mapFlag to 1.0
+        set gpu parameter 63 to mapFlag in holder
+
+# Aims the sun's shadow map at the model (parameters 50 to 61, three rows of
+# four): across and down square to the sun, deep along it toward the model,
+# each 0..1 over a sphere around the model's extent, relative to the scene's
+# origin as the corners are; then draws the model's faces into it (the glass
+# casts none) at the start of the next frame. The sun and the model do not
+# move with the camera, so the map is drawn again only when they change.
+function cast bim shadows of {bim gpu scene record:scene} on {pointer:window}:
+    execute:
+        set context to the gpu context of window
+        set holder to @intrinsic("dereference", context)
+        set towardSun to the bim direction toward the sun
+        set across to the cad cross of (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0) and towardSun
+        if (the cad length of across) < 0.000001:
+            set across to a cad vector3 with x 1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
+        set across to across scaled by (1.0 / (the cad length of across))
+        set down to the cad cross of towardSun and across
+        set inward to towardSun scaled by (0.0 - 1.0)
+        set middle to the cad difference of ((the cad sum of scene's low and scene's high) scaled by 0.5) and scene's origin
+        set reach to the maximum of 1.0 and ((the cad length of (the cad difference of scene's high and scene's low)) * 0.5)
+        set step to 1.0 / (2.0 * reach)
+        set gpu parameter 50 to (across's x * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 51 to (across's y * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 52 to (across's z * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 53 to (0.5 - ((the cad dot of middle and across) * step)) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 54 to (down's x * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 55 to (down's y * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 56 to (down's z * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 57 to (0.5 - ((the cad dot of middle and down) * step)) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 58 to (inward's x * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 59 to (inward's y * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 60 to (inward's z * step) in holder
+        set gpu parameter 61 to (0.5 - ((the cad dot of middle and inward) * step)) in holder
+        cast gpu shadow of slot (bim gpu import slot) from 0 counting scene's importIndexCount in context
